WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:09.160
Fox news is a completely toxic extremist,
right wing echo chamber, mostly sympathetic

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:12.250
to president Donald Trump, but occasionally
not.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:17.460
But every once in a while one of their anchors,
Shepard Smith would tell the truth.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:22.410
He would say what Donald Trump says in this
video, what Donald Trump said in this press

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:24.789
conference is not true.

00:00:24.789 --> 00:00:30.199
He would say, what the Trump administration
is telling you is without evidence, and we

00:00:30.199 --> 00:00:36.660
knew that Shep was out of place this entire
time, but we also recognized it might've been

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:44.370
useful to Fox news to have him there, to provide
ideological cover to allow themselves to say

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:46.370
marginally more credibly.

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:47.740
We are fair and balanced.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:51.300
There is diversity of opinion on our network.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:55.010
And recently it started getting very publicly
ugly.

00:00:55.010 --> 00:01:00.440
For example, Shep Smith, a week or two ago,
interviewed Fox legal analyst, Andrew Nepal,

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:05.820
Caetano, a former judge and Nepal Caetano
said, listen, Trump's actions with Ukraine

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:09.430
are both impeachable and potentially criminal.

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:15.140
Fellow Fox news host, Tucker Carlson came
in and attacked the judge and then Shep and

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:18.840
Tucker got into a public argument that had
to be mediated by Fox news.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:22.510
Higher ups telling Shep Smith, you've got
to it out.

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:27.490
That was a big signal that things were not
looking good for Shep Smith and Shep Smith

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:29.660
has now quit Fox news.

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:33.010
Here's a little bit of him signing off on
his last broadcast.

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:38.750
I've worked with the most talented, dedicated
and focused professionals I've ever known.

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:44.820
They sacrifice endlessly and tirelessly to
get the news exactly right and I am so proud

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:49.130
of them and I'm honored to have anchored their
work each day.

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:54.730
I'll miss them and our time together greatly
and deeply.

00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:59.030
So recently I asked the company to allow me
to leave Fox news after requesting that I

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:01.680
stay, they obliged under our agreement.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:05.700
I won't be reporting elsewhere, at least in
the near future, but I will be able to see

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:10.060
more of geo and Luchea and our friends and
family.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:12.310
Then we'll see what comes along.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:14.430
This is my last newscast here.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:18.940
Thank you for watching today and over the
decades as I traveled to many of your communities

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:24.830
and anchored this program, studio B and Fox
report plus endless marathon hours of breaking

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:25.900
news.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:27.060
It's been an honor.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:31.900
So as Shep says, they're contractually, he's
not allowed to pop up on CNN or MSNBC or ABC

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:33.350
news for some time.

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:35.069
Who knows what he'll be doing financially?

00:02:35.069 --> 00:02:36.069
He's just fine.

00:02:36.069 --> 00:02:38.750
He doesn't have to work probably ever again
if he doesn't want to.

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:40.050
But let's go through this sequentially.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:42.670
First of all, Shep says it was voluntary.

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:48.210
I believe that strictly speaking, it was voluntary,
but it was voluntary in a context where his

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:51.989
boss has had recently come to him and said,
do not go after Tucker Carlson.

00:02:51.989 --> 00:02:57.300
Again, it was happening as president Trump
was increasingly attacking Shepard Smith.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:03.020
It was coming in this context of increased
tension with the broader network because of

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:08.810
his criticisms of Donald Trump and it's pretty
clear that other Fox hosts, we're not expecting

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:09.810
this.

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:15.730
Based on what they said on air, there was
speculation that Shep was pushed out by Trump's

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:17.400
attorney general William Barr.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.099
Now you might say William Barr.

00:03:19.099 --> 00:03:21.220
What on earth is William Barr have to do with
this?

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:28.770
Well, it turns out that the day before Shep's
resignation, William Barr met with a Fox news,

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:32.760
a owner, a news corporation owner, a Rupert
Murdoch.

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:38.700
It is sketchy, but there is no evidence right
now that the meeting was directly related

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:40.209
to Shep Smith.

00:03:40.209 --> 00:03:42.970
So then we get to, is this good or bad?

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:46.930
Because all along I've been saying on the
one hand, Shep telling the truth every once

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:52.640
in awhile might Pierce the echo chamber filter
bubble of the Fox audience and that's a good

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:53.640
thing.

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:58.880
But on the other hand, having at Fox news,
as I mentioned already, gives them some plausible

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:03.700
deniability about being anything other than
tools of the American right wing.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:10.840
I think in the net, the benefits of shepherd
Fox did not outweigh the ideological cover

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:12.870
that he was providing to them.

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:15.690
And especially after becoming a target of
Donald Trump.

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:23.389
Uh, I, I, I understand his decision to do
this whenever he is allowed contractually

00:04:23.389 --> 00:04:27.669
to get back on the air somewhere else, he
is going to be in a great position to advance

00:04:27.669 --> 00:04:28.729
his career.

00:04:28.729 --> 00:04:30.490
Not that that's my primary concern.

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:36.000
I'm guessing he's not going to make as boneheaded
decisions as the ones that Megan Kelly made

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:40.160
when she left Fox news, which basically imploded
her career.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:41.780
That remains to be seen.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:46.850
But there are still lots of Fox viewers who
see this as an unabashed victory.

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:48.080
They hated Shep.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:53.630
They would, anytime he told the truth, start
making homophobic comments about Shep as if

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:58.220
his sexual orientation has anything to do
with whether he's telling us the truth or

00:04:58.220 --> 00:04:59.220
not.

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:01.040
They see him leaving as a victory.

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:06.340
And in a sense for them it may be because
the Fox viewers that are beyond reach, the

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:11.550
ones that are beyond the hope of being pulled
back into considering the reality of the facts

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:16.260
on the ground, they saw Shap as a threat quite
frankly.

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:18.490
And for them Shep leaving is indeed a victory.

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:22.120
So not surprising probably in the net.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:27.440
Uh, something that is not going to have any
kind of real impact on the 2020 election or

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:30.620
on Donald Trump, but not a surprising thing.

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:34.970
As we've been following for a couple of years
now and we will see where Shep lands and we

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:35.970
will see.

00:05:35.970 --> 00:05:39.229
Interestingly also, will there be any, you
know, Trump has also been going after Chris

00:05:39.229 --> 00:05:45.770
Wallace who less frequently than Shep, but
every once in awhile we'll insert some truth

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:50.300
into his broadcasts or his challenging questions
to Trump officials.

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:52.389
Is Chris Wallace the next target?

00:05:52.389 --> 00:05:56.090
If you look at Trump's Twitter over the last
couple of days, you see that the answer is

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:57.100
probably yes.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:57.569
Chris Wallace is the next target.

